---
import Explainer from '../../components/Explainer.astro'
import { components } from '../../data/components.js'
import { diagrams } from '../../data/diagrams.js'
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/paths.js'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · suitecut"
  description="What suitecut is, how its embedded Chromium works, and the native components it ships."
  current="about"
>
  <article class="page prose about">
    <h1>About suitecut</h1>
    <p class="about-lede">
      suitecut is an embedded Chromium built to be recorded, streamed and driven. It is native code:
      a CEF engine, a C++ SDK with a C ABI, a command line that is also an MCP server, and a kit for
      putting the engine inside a Mac app.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what">What it does</h2>
    <dl class="about-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Record</dt>
        <dd>
          Capture what the page really draws and plays into WebM, or hardware H.264 MP4 on macOS,
          with counts of every real and held frame.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Stream</dt>
        <dd>Publish the same pixels and sound live over RTMP, RTMPS or TCP.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Drive</dt>
        <dd>
          Control the browser from C++, C, a command line or any MCP client, or point the same tools
          at the Chrome or Firefox you already have.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Embed</dt>
        <dd>
          Show the engine's tabs in your own macOS app, with frames on the GPU, and let an agent
          work in the same tabs.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
    <p>
      suitecut ships its own Chromium Embedded Framework runtime, pinned to CEF 156.0.30. Video
      comes straight from the renderer's paint callback and audio from its audio stream, so there's
      no screenshot loop, browser extension or open debugging port in the capture path.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your code talks to the engine over a pipe: JSON commands in, binary packets out. Frames and
      sound flow back on one clock, where the recorder picks the newest real image for each output
      frame and never blends or invents motion. FFmpeg encodes the result into a file or a live
      stream.
    </p>
    <p>
      The C++ SDK, the C ABI, the agent tools and the MCP server sit on one native library. In an
      embedding app, the person and the agent share one session, with the same pages, cookies and
      storage, and take turns on each tab.
    </p>
    <Explainer explained={diagrams.together} />

    <h2 id="components">Components</h2>
    <div class="about-packages">
      {
        components.map((item) => (
          <div>
            <p class="about-package-name">
              <strong>
                <a href={sitePath(`/components/${item.slug}`)}>{item.name}</a>
              </strong>
              <span>{item.kind}</span>
            </p>
            <p class="about-package-text">{item.line}.</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <h2 id="status">Where things stand</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The current version is 0.1.1, an alpha for macOS ARM64 and the line's second native-only
        release. Interfaces can still change before 1.0.
      </li>
      <li>
        Linux x64 builds from source but wasn't tested for 0.1.1. Windows runtime packaging isn't
        implemented yet.
      </li>
      <li>
        Nothing is published to a package registry. The
        <a href={sitePath('/docs#release')}>0.1.1 alpha's</a> SDK archives, embed kit and full runtime
        are a GitHub pre-release, signed but not notarized yet.
      </li>
      <li>
        The earlier Node.js packages, including the npm package and the video renderer, were removed
        on 2026-11-22.
      </li>
      <li>
        Every published <a href={sitePath('/benchmarks')}>benchmark</a> names its host, commit and the
        command that reproduces it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="open-source">Open source</h2>
    <p>
      suitecut is MIT licensed and developed in the open on
      <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut">GitHub</a>. Read the
      <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">contributing guide</a> to
      get involved, and report security issues through the
      <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/SECURITY.md">security policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-lede {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    line-height: 2rem;
  }

  .about-list,
  .about-packages {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .about-list div,
  .about-packages > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 14rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .about-list dt {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }

  .about-list dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .about-packages p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-package-name {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .about-package-name a {
    color: inherit;
  }

  .about-package-name strong {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .about-package-name span {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .about-package-text {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .about-list div,
    .about-packages > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }

    .about-package-name {
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
      align-items: center;
    }
  }
</style>
